{:edb/db-before-t 1114 :edb/db-after-t 1115 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534427 50 #inst "2026-10-07T02:46:57.690Z" 13194139534427 true] [17592186100805 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287689 13194139534427 true] [17592186100871 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287675 13194139534427 true] [17592186100871 1020 #edb/ref 17592186287682 13194139534427 true] [17592186101018 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534427 true] [17592186101018 1100 "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nThe coefficient of $x^{7}$ in the expansion of $(4 + x)^{9}$ is" 13194139534427 false] [17592186101018 1100 "The coefficient of ${x}^{7}$ in the expansion of ${(4+x)}^{9}$ is" 13194139534427 true] [17592186101018 1145 "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n \n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\frac{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\frac{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\frac{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(4+x)}^{9},$ we have $a=4,$ $b=x,$ and $n=9.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4+x)^{9}=(\\frac{9}{0}){4}^{9}{x}^{0}+(\\frac{9}{1}){4}^{9-1}{x}^{1}+(\\frac{9}{2}){4}^{9-2}{x}^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{9}{9}){4}^{9-9}{x}^{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the ${x}^{7}$ term must be\n\n$$\n(\\frac{9}{7}){4}^{9-7}{x}^{7}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating the coefficient, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{9}{7}){4}^{9-7} & =36\\cdot {4}^{2} \\\\  & =36\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =576.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${x}^{7}$ is $576.$" 13194139534427 true] [17592186101052 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534427 true] [17592186101052 1100 "$(4-x)^{4}=$" 13194139534427 true] [17592186101052 1100 "What is $(4 - x)^{4}$?" 13194139534427 false] [17592186101052 1145 "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n \n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\frac{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\frac{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\frac{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+⋯+(\\frac{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of $(4-x)^{4},$ we have  $a=4,$ $b=-x,$ $n=4.$ \n\nTherefore, the first three terms of $(4-x)^{4}$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(4-x)}^{4} & =(\\frac{4}{0}){(4)}^{4}{(-x)}^{0}+(\\frac{4}{1}){(4)}^{4-1}{(-x)}^{1}+(\\frac{4}{2}){(4)}^{4-2}{(-x)}^{2}+… \\\\  & =1{(4)}^{4}+4{(4)}^{3}{(-x)}^{1}+6{(4)}^{2}{(-x)}^{2}+… \\\\  & =256-256x+96{x}^{2}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534427 true] [17592186287675 1017 #edb/ref 17592186287676 13194139534427 true] [17592186287675 1089 "q-12841" 13194139534427 true] [17592186287675 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534427 true] [17592186287675 1100 "${(s-t)}^{9}=$" 13194139534427 true] [17592186287675 1113 #uuid "26d64e14-48be-5cd9-8f9a-40fbb0ecc51d" 13194139534427 true] [17592186287675 1145 "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n \n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\frac{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\frac{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\frac{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+…+(\\frac{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(s-t)}^{9},$ we have  $a=s,$ $b=-t,$ $n=9.$ \n\nTherefore, the first three terms of ${(s-t)}^{9}$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(s-t)}^{9} & =(\\frac{9}{0}){(s)}^{9}{(-t)}^{0}+(\\frac{9}{1}){(s)}^{9-1}{(-t)}^{1}+(\\frac{9}{2}){(s)}^{9-2}{(-t)}^{2}+… \\\\  & =1{(s)}^{9}+9{(s)}^{8}{(-t)}^{1}+36{(s)}^{7}{(-t)}^{2}+… \\\\  & =1({s}^{9})+9({s}^{8})(-t)+36({s}^{7})({t}^{2})+… \\\\  & ={s}^{9}-9{s}^{8}t+36{s}^{7}{t}^{2}+…\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534427 true] [17592186287676 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287677 13194139534427 true] [17592186287676 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287678 13194139534427 true] [17592186287676 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287679 13194139534427 true] [17592186287676 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287680 13194139534427 true] [17592186287676 1000 #edb/ref 17592186287681 13194139534427 true] [17592186287676 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534427 true] [17592186287676 1041 "selection" 13194139534427 true] [17592186287676 1104 #edb/ref 17592186287679 13194139534427 true] [17592186287676 1110 #uuid "4b7d6e8e-1512-50b5-8b71-265233f37486" 1319413953